# Trivy misreads pip's internal build-dependency manifest
# (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt) as if setuptools and msgpack were installed,
# top-level, independently-reachable packages. Neither is, verified by
# inspecting the built image directly:
#
#   - setuptools' code isn't present anywhere in the image. pip only
#     references its pinned version as the build backend it WOULD fall back
#     to if it ever needed to build a package from source — never triggered
#     here since requirements.txt installs entirely from prebuilt wheels.
#   - msgpack IS vendored, but privately inside pip's own internals
#     (pip/_vendor/msgpack), used only by pip's own HTTP cache during
#     `pip install`. Never imported by this app, and never reachable at
#     container runtime since pip isn't invoked after the image is built.
#
# Re-check with a fresh build + `find / -iname '*setuptools*'` /
# `find / -iname '*msgpack*'` before removing these — the right fix is
# pip itself bumping its own vendored pins, not something addressable here.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890
